    {
      "name": "Cryptidkin Heritage: Furrykin",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "art/bbttcc/GOTTGAIT/BBTTCC_Character_Options/RayCat.png",
      "system": {
        "category": "technique",
        "source": "Bad Eden (2024 rules)",
        "tags": [],
        "description": {
          "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><strong>Cryptidkin Subspecies.</strong> This heritage preserves the original UUID for <em>Furrykin</em> while converting it from a species-root with five sub-clades into a single flexible Cryptidkin subspecies.</p><p><em>“You are not an animal that learned to talk. You are a person the world made with fur because it needed you to survive.”</em></p><p><strong>Furrykin.</strong> You are anything fur-bearing the world decided to make people out of. Talking badger, cunning fox, stoic bear, watchful rabbit, the uncle-shaped thing the trappers call Bigfoot—all valid. Size and frame are flexible; the instinct is not.</p><h3>Traits</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Creature Type.</strong> Humanoid (Cryptidkin).</p></li><li><p><strong>Size.</strong> Small or Medium (choose at creation; Medium Furrykin can describe themselves as “large and shaggy” without mechanical change—Bigfoot-scale creatures still move and fight at Medium).</p></li><li><p><strong>Speed.</strong> 6 squares</p></li><li><p><strong>Subspecies Lean.</strong> No fixed stat lean. Your frame is your business—the Tier powers adapt to how you play it.</p></li></ul><h3>Core: Folklore & Frame</h3><p>At creation you gain <strong>Folklore & Frame</strong> (Folklore Presence, Wasteland Adapted, Survivor’s Instinct).</p><h3>Wildframe & Instinct (Furrykin Extras)</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Wildframe.</strong> Your body is built for a world that bites back. You already reroll the lowest die on checks against disease and environmental poison (from Wasteland Adapted); as Furrykin, you also add your tier to any Body defense check to resist Stress.</p></li><li><p><strong>Keen Sense.</strong> Choose one: <em>Keen Smell</em>, <em>Keen Hearing</em>, or <em>Keen Sight</em>. You reroll the lowest die on Perception checks relying on that sense.</p></li><li><p><strong>Frame Choice.</strong> Choose one narrative frame at creation: <em>Predator</em> (bite or claws count as unarmed strikes that deal 1d6 instead of 1d4), <em>Forager</em> (trained in Athletics), or <em>Brute</em> (count as one size larger for carrying, shoving, and grappling).</p></li></ul><h3>Furrykin Tier Powers</h3><p>You gain Tier I at creation, then Tier II (5), Tier III (11), Tier IV (17). Tier powers previously split across Felid / Leporid / Mustelid / Ursid / Vulpin are unified; choose flavor at the table without mechanical separation.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
